{"duration_api_ms":66720,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"132d8c13-163b-47b2-a046-5d716fb2d7ce","total_cost_usd":0.200029,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32121,"cache_read_input_tokens":47385,"output_tokens":6206,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1167},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32121,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2537,"cache_read_input_tokens":37845,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3816,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3816},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":6206,"cacheReadInputTokens":47385,"cacheCreationInputTokens":32121,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.200029,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":1167,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"https-8443\",\"requirement\":\"Serve HTTPS on node1 port 8443\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"nginx installed, configured with an https-8443.conf server block listening on 0.0.0.0:8443 and [::]:8443, config validated with nginx -t, service enabled and active, firewalld port 8443/tcp opened permanently, and curl over TLS returned http_code=200. Confirmed again in the post-reboot after_executor listening-sockets snapshot showing nginx bound to 8443 on both IPv4/IPv6.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e16d390a866a4230\",\"cmd-9387412e11e14455\",\"cmd-fbb1dff5e9ae4968\",\"cmd-5bb97a730fcd4ab6\",\"global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets\"]},{\"id\":\"cert-auto-renewal\",\"requirement\":\"Certificate is renewed automatically before it expires\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A systemd oneshot service (cert-renew.service) driven by a 60s-interval timer (cert-renew.timer) runs renew-cert.sh, which checks certificate validity via `openssl x509 -checkend 180` and reissues a new self-signed cert when fewer than 180s of a deliberately short (6-minute) lifetime remain. Two independent automatic renewals were directly observed: one before reboot (serial changed from 5E40A9F5... to 4B4F3527..., notAfter extended, logged in /var/log/renew-cert.log at 10:04:39) and one after reboot (serial changed to 25112A49..., notAfter extended to 14:13:51, logged at 10:07:51), each occurring without manual intervention.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7fa528522ea74c8e\",\"cmd-0d239e5ca67d4a8b\",\"cmd-e6d7d2951d1a413d\",\"cmd-f9b9fff3d0bf45fa\"]},{\"id\":\"service-picks-up-cert\",\"requirement\":\"Service picks up each new certificate while continuing to answer requests\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"renew-cert.sh issues `systemctl reload nginx` (guarded by an is-active check) after swapping in the new cert/key, which is a zero-downtime reload. Immediately after the pre-reboot renewal, curl to :8443 still returned 200 and a live TLS handshake via openssl s_client served the exact new serial (4B4F3527...), and the same pattern held after the post-reboot renewal (serial 25112A49..., http_code=200), directly demonstrating continuous service while the certificate rotated underneath it.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-0d239e5ca67d4a8b\",\"cmd-d7f77e35d02f4f3c\",\"cmd-e6d7d2951d1a413d\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-evidence-protocol\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on node1 (independent of task contract)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart baseline captured boot_id 83a0a80f..., nginx/cert-renew.timer active, HTTPS 200, live cert serial matching the renewed cert. `systemctl reboot` was issued and acknowledged (backgrounded). After connection drops/timeouts consistent with a real reboot, a new boot_id (ee5486d2...) was observed, matching the fixed after_executor global snapshot. Post-reboot, nginx and cert-renew.timer were both active again, HTTPS served 200 with the persisted cert, and a fresh automatic renewal occurred and was served live over TLS post-recovery — showing the full pre-restart/disruption/post-restart/recovered-state transition for services, data (cert files), and cluster/automation state.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-a95a2943d2474f8a\",\"cmd-2251d467984f4d4a\",\"cmd-cbb70143a7174e77\",\"cmd-ff5d6d8129484d87\",\"cmd-a4e0baf310e54dd3\",\"cmd-e6d7d2951d1a413d\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.94,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.95,\"summary\":\"Reviewed all state-changing executor commands chronologically: package install, iterative writes of renew-cert.sh (three revisions, each a deliberate refinement — checkend threshold tightened, notAfter switched to a fixed short lifetime, reload guarded with is-active — not abandoned experiments), node.env creation, manual first-run of the script to seed the initial cert (necessary prerequisite before nginx could start with TLS), nginx config/service enablement, firewalld port opening, and systemd unit creation for the timer. Every mutation maps directly to a required outcome or a necessary prerequisite; none were reverted-but-unnecessary troubleshooting. The reboot (cmd-2251d467984f4d4a) was the mandated restart-evidence action. Minor residue: /tmp/renew-cert.log (openssl req output redirect inside the script) and /tmp/reboot.log (nohup output) were left in place — both are small, low-risk operational log artifacts with a clear causal role (script diagnostics, reboot scheduling) rather than unrelated debris, so severity is low. No failed services, no damaged package state, and firewalld/socket changes match the intended 8443 exposure with no unnecessary port openings.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-fb6a0ffa753f49b8\",\"cmd-5928d67b9c3b4545\",\"cmd-3578362e52e04ef3\",\"cmd-cb2944285d7f4175\",\"cmd-6230e527361c4605\",\"cmd-f9b9fff3d0bf45fa\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All three material outcomes of the task — HTTPS on 8443, automatic pre-expiry certificate renewal, and gapless pickup of each new certificate — are directly and repeatedly demonstrated in the evidence, including across a full node reboot. The independent restart-evidence protocol is also fully satisfied with matching boot-identity snapshots and confirmed post-reboot recovery of nginx, the renewal timer, and live TLS serving. No unnecessary or unreverted risky mutations were found; only trivial log-file residue remains.\",\"limitations\":[\"The 6-minute certificate lifetime and 180s checkend threshold are executor-chosen test parameters for demonstrability within the session; longer-lived production certificates were not exercised, though the renewal mechanism itself is lifetime-agnostic.\",\"One long-poll command (cmd-3e63502a0f4545d7) failed due to a proxy read timeout rather than a service failure; it was immediately followed by a successful equivalent check (cmd-a4e0baf310e54dd3), so it does not indicate an outage.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"https-8443","requirement":"Serve HTTPS on node1 port 8443","status":"satisfied","summary":"nginx installed, configured with an https-8443.conf server block listening on 0.0.0.0:8443 and [::]:8443, config validated with nginx -t, service enabled and active, firewalld port 8443/tcp opened permanently, and curl over TLS 