al log artifacts with a clear causal role (script diagnostics, reboot scheduling) rather than unrelated debris, so severity is low. No failed services, no damaged package state, and firewalld/socket changes match the intended 8443 exposure with no unnecessary port openings.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fb6a0ffa753f49b8","cmd-5928d67b9c3b4545","cmd-3578362e52e04ef3","cmd-cb2944285d7f4175","cmd-6230e527361c4605","cmd-f9b9fff3d0bf45fa","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All three material outcomes of the task — HTTPS on 8443, automatic pre-expiry certificate renewal, and gapless pickup of each new certificate — are directly and repeatedly demonstrated in the evidence, including across a full node reboot. The independent restart-evidence protocol is also fully satisfied with matching boot-identity snapshots and confirmed post-reboot recovery of nginx, the renewal timer, and live TLS serving. No unnecessary or unreverted risky mutations were found; only trivial log-file residue remains.","limitations":["The 6-minute certificate lifetime and 180s checkend threshold are executor-chosen test parameters for demonstrability within the session; longer-lived production certificates were not exercised, though the renewal mechanism itself is lifetime-agnostic.","One long-poll command (cmd-3e63502a0f4545d7) failed due to a proxy read timeout rather than a service failure; it was immediately followed by a successful equivalent check (cmd-a4e0baf310e54dd3), so it does not indicate an outage."]},"ttft_ms":19403,"type":"result","duration_ms":66913,"uuid":"b6e8f224-7a45-4bd8-9386-c4756a2718e5","ttft_stream_ms":2250,"time_to_request_ms":181,"first_content_frame_ms":2250,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
